  "summary": {
    "en": "Insurgent militants have continued to disrupt infrastructure, stealing a transformer at Lichinga Airport and prompting the shutdown of the Metoro solar plant, which authorities are now working to restore. Mozambican security forces captured six alleged terrorists in Macomia while the United States considers training Mozambican special forces as Islamic State threatens regional shipping. A trial has begun for opposition leader Venâncio Mondlane, reflecting heightened political tension amid the conflict. A baobab tree fell on homes in Namutequeliua, Nampula, killing two women, illustrating broader insecurity. There were 151 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
